{"id": "EUVD-2026-89187", "enisaUuid": "626c873d-b1d1-32f6-981c-f23a43f3963b", "description": "In the IPv4 PASV path, the FTP Client accepts whatever address was sent in the server's `227` reply. Validation only covers the parse and the non-zero values, thus a malicious server can name any address and direct the Client there.", "datePublished": "2026-09-29T17:47:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T18:34:41", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-threadx/netxduo/security/advisories/GHSA-j6g2-8fm3-rm8m"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p9rr-8wmf-9r7v", "CVE-2026-102722"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b41bac54-ee51-3a74-80c8-911a753f1182", "product": {"name": "NetX Duo", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.5.1.202602"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8921d9e9-cc9b-3e9a-86cb-2256fd90e366", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}